--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- submerged Rigid6 buoy on a three-leg taut polyester mooring, current, dynamic
-- A net-buoyant 6-DOF rigid buoy (20 t, 40 m^3 displaced) is held 20 m below the surface in 100 m
-- of water by three taut polyester legs at 120 deg. Each leg runs from a Body1 attachment 1.5 m off
-- the buoy axis and 2 m below its reference point (End A) to a seabed anchor at radius 40 m (End B).
-- The body is free in all six degrees of freedom: line loads and the lumped buoyancy, drag (CdA),
-- and added mass (Ca) set its motion. A 0.6 m/s uniform current in +X loads the buoy and legs.
-- Rigid6 bodies require a dynamic deck (dtM and TMax). The default bodyIC static starts the buoy
-- at its equilibrium in the current, displaced downstream until the legs balance the drag, and the
-- run holds that position. The body, its attachment points and its lines advance together in the
-- default monolithic implicit step (bodyScheme monolithic); the outputs are the same to six
-- digits at dtM = 0.005, 0.01 and 0.1 s.
